$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\ln(3x)}{e^{7x}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\ln(3x)\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[e^{7x}]}\qquad\gray{\text{l’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{3}{3x}\right)}{7e^{7x}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{1}{7xe^{7x}}
\\\\
&=0
\end{align}$

Note that we were only able to use l’Hôpital’s rule because the limit $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\ln(3x)\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[e^{7x}]}$ can actually be determined.
